#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171848 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172042 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca277aab-fe4b-57a0-8d86-3b08bded62c8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Mean Values in Context"}] :question/id #uuid "904ea623-83b3-54e3-a685-1ec83bbce877" :question/math-academy-id "e-8617" :question/problem "A fair die has $12$ sides labeled with numbers $1$ through $12.$ What is the expected value of a random roll of this die?" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the number the die lands on. From the problem statement, we know that $X \\sim U \\{1, 2, \\ldots, 12\\},$ and we wish to compute $\\textrm E[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X \\sim U \\{a, a + 1, \\ldots, b\\},$ then $X$ has the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\dfrac{a+b}{2}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X \\sim U \\{ 1, 2, \\ldots, 12\\},$ we have the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\dfrac{1+12}{2} = 6.5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expected value is $6.5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171849 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172043 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "71b53035-4d10-575b-a18c-d88c944d0884" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Variances in Context"}] :question/id #uuid "bff23e5c-8b98-5147-9966-97b5da1c1759" :question/math-academy-id "e-8618" :question/problem "A fair die has sides labeled with numbers $4$ through $15.$ What is the variance of the numbers obtained when rolling this die?" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the number the die lands on. From the problem statement, we know that $X \\sim U \\{ 4, 5, \\ldots, 15 \\},$ and we wish to compute $\\textrm{Var}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X \\sim U \\{a, a + 1, \\ldots, b\\},$ then the variance of $X$ is\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = \\dfrac{|S|^2-1}{12}\n$$\n\nwhere $S = \\{a, a+1, \\ldots, b\\}.$\n\nNow, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|S| & =b-a+1 \\\\  & =15-4+1 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X \\sim U \\{ 4, 5, \\ldots, 15 \\},$ we have the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X] = \\dfrac{12^2 - 1}{12} = \\dfrac{143}{12}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance is $\\dfrac{143}{12}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523926 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172042 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca277aab-fe4b-57a0-8d86-3b08bded62c8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Mean Values in Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23e62e66-6874-55ab-ba69-892301b35036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{29}^{∘}C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523325} {:answer/id #uuid "41105bc3-efc1-57ce-a685-dc34b23250d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523388} {:answer/id #uuid "5b7ffb64-ed8a-5f80-9ea2-8337e02eab71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30.5}^{∘}C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523440} {:answer/id #uuid "8e8c9b42-2856-5eca-b358-7f3a1c9bfbf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{31.5}^{∘}C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523550} {:answer/id #uuid "b79d5078-8977-524a-9cd8-7811d81ebe23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{29.5}^{∘}C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b7ffb64-ed8a-5f80-9ea2-8337e02eab71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30.5}^{∘}C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523440} :answer-field/id #uuid "fee83434-bea6-5d24-8061-9f7887df13cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523920}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "061c757d-590b-5605-a6a4-5e9539c29dc6" :question/math-academy-id "q-149461" :question/problem "In summer, the daily maximum temperature in a particular city (rounded to the nearest degree) varies between ${25}^{∘}C$ and ${36}^{∘}C,$ inclusive. Assuming that each maximum temperature value has the same probability of occurring on a given summer day, what is the expected value of the daily maximum temperature?" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the daily maximum temperature (rounded to the nearest degree) on a randomly selected day. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U\\{25,26,…,36\\},$ and we wish to compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U\\{a,a+1,…,b\\},$ then $X$ has the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{a+b}{2}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U\\{25,26,…,36\\},$ we have the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{25+36}{2}=30.5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expected value of the maximum temperature is ${30.5}^{∘}C.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524029 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172042 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca277aab-fe4b-57a0-8d86-3b08bded62c8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Mean Values in Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c5fd90f-c90f-54ef-8a7e-37270bd09def" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523381} {:answer/id #uuid "445cdad2-f731-5550-954e-5375b1603f59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523396} {:answer/id #uuid "50706252-4cc9-5b73-a0a1-41411c3dfaf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523417} {:answer/id #uuid "76a7eda3-f8be-53a8-8129-8e4f2f5b435d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523497} {:answer/id #uuid "79275914-5d9c-5c8c-82f4-240ddc318b56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79275914-5d9c-5c8c-82f4-240ddc318b56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523501} :answer-field/id #uuid "73b46de2-2050-5a32-a2b1-20ea872f37a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e9910a94-d71d-54e3-8cb5-b52ba8bdfed9" :question/math-academy-id "q-149467" :question/problem "In a math test, students have to answer a multiple-choice question, where the answers are labeled from $0$ to $6.$ If Steph selects an answer at random, what is the expected value of her chosen answer?" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the number of the chosen answer. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U\\{0,1,…,6\\},$ and we wish to compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U\\{a,a+1,…,b\\},$ then $X$ has the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{a+b}{2}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U\\{0,1,…,6\\},$ we have the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{0+6}{2}=3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expected value of the chosen answer is $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523955 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172043 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "71b53035-4d10-575b-a18c-d88c944d0884" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Variances in Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6bd67d5-7c1f-5c2c-9a46-0ef1a20e4c70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523605} {:answer/id #uuid "ca6903e7-fb79-5a78-beff-0b8e832b93a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523675} {:answer/id #uuid "e4b719eb-6ae8-58bf-9dac-72caecc590b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523733} {:answer/id #uuid "f65db99c-57e5-5e25-8db1-cffb700d0d10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523769} {:answer/id #uuid "fae0d576-f0f9-50db-9357-1c4257578253" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.05" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523779}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6bd67d5-7c1f-5c2c-9a46-0ef1a20e4c70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523605} :answer-field/id #uuid "03d527bc-ebb6-5c35-b1e7-c65135d3ef4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523791}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "56f939dc-3462-5544-b92f-c768cb817339" :question/math-academy-id "q-149510" :question/problem "A spinner divided into eight equal sections numbered $2$ through $9$ is spun. What is the variance of the numbers obtained?" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the number obtained by spinning the spinner. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U\\{2,3,…,9\\},$ and we wish to compute $\\text{Var}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U\\{a,a+1,…,b\\},$ then the variance of $X$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{|S{|}^{2}-1}{12}\n$$\n\nwhere $S=\\{a,a+1,…,b\\}.$\n\nNow, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|S| & =b-a+1 \\\\  & =9-2+1 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U\\{2,3,…,9\\},$ we have the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{{8}^{2}-1}{12}=\\frac{63}{12}=5.25\n$$\n\nTherefore, the variance of the numbers obtained is $5.25$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523952 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172042 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca277aab-fe4b-57a0-8d86-3b08bded62c8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Mean Values in Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15942d05-c04c-5fec-acfd-214aa02bd9e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "47" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523301} {:answer/id #uuid "300ddeda-7b55-5f6f-89a4-743bae59195a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "46" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523355} {:answer/id #uuid "5f3dc81f-5e80-5290-a8f3-71e8b20db9e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523447} {:answer/id #uuid "80779f00-66da-5d77-9263-f46efafd4786" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "46.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523527} {:answer/id #uuid "cd8f4bb4-6117-5ad7-b11c-5e92b496e511" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "47.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523682}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80779f00-66da-5d77-9263-f46efafd4786" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "46.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523527} :answer-field/id #uuid "64f16db9-01e1-5022-b628-d7fb9a1a158c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523838}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4dac21a9-fd23-5a65-b9b0-0999f6a3ac35" :question/math-academy-id "q-97653" :question/problem "Ann chooses a card at random from a deck of cards labeled $28$ through $65.$  What is the expected value of the chosen number?" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the value of the number chosen. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U\\{28,29,…,65\\},$ and we wish to compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U\\{a,a+1,…,b\\},$ then $X$ has the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{a+b}{2}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U\\{28,29,…,65\\},$ we have the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{28+65}{2}=46.5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expected value of the chosen number is $46.5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523932 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172042 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca277aab-fe4b-57a0-8d86-3b08bded62c8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Mean Values in Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05f16bfe-9d21-56eb-b0eb-cf81ad7da361" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523267} {:answer/id #uuid "2eb2d4ce-443f-5483-8106-4785809a785f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523350} {:answer/id #uuid "42fc9fab-ee26-5c8e-8118-2f6cb80a2248" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523391} {:answer/id #uuid "7d4d83a3-f6df-5c00-9cba-9e140b768621" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523517} {:answer/id #uuid "e9d487b6-ed79-5dc1-ab39-7e81e4eb1566" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42fc9fab-ee26-5c8e-8118-2f6cb80a2248" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523391} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8e0d0aa-1c21-5a25-b57e-4af99d80d340" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523915}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "17dce6e5-6992-5bd8-99ae-27a5145f8ae5" :question/math-academy-id "q-97661" :question/problem "Jack wants to buy a single issue of a particular comic series with $70$ issues. Unfortunately, the comic store does not have the first $10$ issues in stock. If Jack buys a comic at random from the available issues, what is the expected value of the chosen issue?" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the number of the selected issue. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U\\{11,12…,70\\},$ and we wish to compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U\\{a,a+1,…,b\\},$ then $X$ has the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{a+b}{2}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U\\{11,12,…,70\\},$ we have the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{11+70}{2}=40.5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expected value of the chosen number is $40.5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524014 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172043 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "71b53035-4d10-575b-a18c-d88c944d0884" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Variances in Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a1203d0-1e7b-54e5-8193-b827f429d9cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18.33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523275} {:answer/id #uuid "481a7a00-f069-5a6a-8af6-970d5cab079e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13.85" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523402} {:answer/id #uuid "5cabcbf3-2946-56f9-90a0-75fe304c4571" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10.42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523444} {:answer/id #uuid "82a3d961-1417-5f80-8d5c-e3c1b0544af2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14.85" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523531} {:answer/id #uuid "ecd40b35-713e-5902-b659-478c76c266f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11.52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523750}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "481a7a00-f069-5a6a-8af6-970d5cab079e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13.85" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523402} :answer-field/id #uuid "81f39eb4-0d43-54f8-9984-4333850219c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523855}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d0deae3f-c105-5c17-970a-aab6db3301cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-97662" :question/problem "Jack wants to buy a single issue of a particular comic series with $55$ issues. Unfortunately, the comic store does not have the first $7$ issues in stock. If Jack buys a comic at random from the available issues, what is the standard deviation of the issue numbers he could select? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the number of the issue Jack selects. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U\\{8,9,…,55\\},$ and we wish to compute $\\text{SD}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U\\{a,a+1,…,b\\},$ then the variance of $X$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{|S{|}^{2}-1}{12}\n$$\n\nwhere $S=\\{a,a+1,…,b\\}.$\n\nNow, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|S| & =b-a+1 \\\\  & =55-8+1 \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U\\{8,9,…,55\\},$ we have the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{{48}^{2}-1}{12}=\\frac{2303}{12}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\frac{2303}{12}}≈13.85.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523936 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172043 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "71b53035-4d10-575b-a18c-d88c944d0884" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Variances in Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28d54e01-612b-51a9-95d4-bf586e1dafa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.89" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523338} {:answer/id #uuid "7a77fed5-2ba6-529c-b2b4-c567b5738f39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523506} {:answer/id #uuid "a125b2c6-d0e3-5bca-82a7-a665091f0a9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523590} {:answer/id #uuid "a38f5599-d61b-5a09-a3d4-9a183da4b04f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523599} {:answer/id #uuid "a3e11fdc-0c7e-5f9a-89ed-ed5da8b344d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523600}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a38f5599-d61b-5a09-a3d4-9a183da4b04f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523599} :answer-field/id #uuid "869e1747-44a9-5a0c-bf12-3ac41ecf6be3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523859}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1e997cfb-3847-52d2-9127-67ab63d15dde" :question/math-academy-id "q-97677" :question/problem "A traditional festival is usually held on a single day after the $6$th and before the $15$th of September. The exact day is selected each year and depends on the weather conditions. Assuming that each day after the $6$th and before the $15$th of September has the same probability of being chosen, what is the standard deviation of the selected days? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the date of the selected day. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U\\{7,8,…,14\\},$ and we wish to compute $\\text{SD}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U\\{a,a+1,…,b\\},$ then the variance of $X$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{|S{|}^{2}-1}{12}\n$$\n\nwhere $S=\\{a,a+1,…,b\\}.$\n\nNow, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|S| & =b-a+1 \\\\  & =14-7+1 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U\\{7,8,…,14\\},$ we have the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{{8}^{2}-1}{12}=\\frac{63}{12}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\frac{63}{12}}≈2.29.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524039 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172042 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca277aab-fe4b-57a0-8d86-3b08bded62c8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Mean Values in Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bb18bb9-04e6-5364-9edf-e9f090bde6b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523279} {:answer/id #uuid "20cf2347-734c-59f0-8d38-4914b0f59872" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523318} {:answer/id #uuid "443997de-1648-5657-9a9f-fbd252621d6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523395} {:answer/id #uuid "6fd9a2fd-6bfa-526d-85b1-51dc29c80930" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523483} {:answer/id #uuid "7d2ad557-2ff4-5a06-8c6b-c2198562c980" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523516}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d2ad557-2ff4-5a06-8c6b-c2198562c980" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523516} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5e331db-3e94-5f66-9647-04d18ac848fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523871}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f8cca8da-6044-5230-8f59-af0159f2bec9" :question/math-academy-id "q-97686" :question/problem "Lucy's marbles are labeled with numbers $-3$ through $8.$ If Lucy chooses a marble at random, what is the expected value of the chosen marble?" :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the number on the chosen marble. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U\\{-3,-2,…,8\\},$ and we wish to compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U\\{a,a+1,…,b\\},$ then $X$ has the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{a+b}{2}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U\\{-3,-2,…,8\\},$ we have the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{-3+8}{2}=2.5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expected value of the chosen marble is $2.5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523938 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172043 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "71b53035-4d10-575b-a18c-d88c944d0884" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Variances in Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f9a88d8-ca73-5ff5-8ab0-35488e393aea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523386} {:answer/id #uuid "6f424c05-1480-5131-af5e-6301d6c236d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.87" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523482} {:answer/id #uuid "79caa7ce-46ad-55e2-b7c2-043a0fad8141" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523504} {:answer/id #uuid "7eedec42-febe-5b57-bb9d-ded0c88caada" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523522} {:answer/id #uuid "c5edd35f-5e6f-5071-859d-b0ea47da1df0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f424c05-1480-5131-af5e-6301d6c236d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.87" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523482} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cf40b77-3ab5-59b6-90e4-0f17d078e3d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523820}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2200f2ed-00f4-5dc2-a53c-43c556e4cd84" :question/math-academy-id "q-97687" :question/problem "Lucy's marbles are labeled with numbers $0$ through $9.$ If Lucy chooses a marble at random, what is the standard deviation of the numbers of the selected marbles? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the number of the chosen marble. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U\\{0,1,…,9\\},$ and we wish to compute $\\text{SD}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U\\{a,a+1,…,b\\},$ then the variance of $X$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{|S{|}^{2}-1}{12}\n$$\n\nwhere $S=\\{a,a+1,…,b\\}.$\n\nNow, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|S| & =b-a+1 \\\\  & =9-0+1 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U\\{0,1,…,9\\},$ we have the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{{10}^{2}-1}{12}=\\frac{99}{12}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\frac{99}{12}}≈2.87.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523957 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172043 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "71b53035-4d10-575b-a18c-d88c944d0884" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Variances in Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10213f2b-2013-52dd-8671-4f8389a29c25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14.12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523288} {:answer/id #uuid "773abe72-877b-5c5e-bf53-c3b27d4edd5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11.20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523498} {:answer/id #uuid "ae12b462-1a1a-5233-90f4-ad10dc2f9177" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15.36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523620} {:answer/id #uuid "b162a2b7-4a87-587f-adb8-e0ce9c946199" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13.28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523628} {:answer/id #uuid "bf2423de-5d8a-5b6f-866d-ecbbbc5a1ac5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13.86" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b162a2b7-4a87-587f-adb8-e0ce9c946199" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13.28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523628} :answer-field/id #uuid "acd72576-8d1e-5c1b-9d00-62b65f8647c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523874}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "57d50a92-18de-56e3-a7c3-f6f999c0fbca" :question/math-academy-id "q-97695" :question/problem "In a video game, the number of obstacles that show up during a game can vary between $80$ and $125,$ inclusive. Assuming that each number of obstacles has the same probability of occurring, what is the standard deviation of the number of obstacles? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let $X$ represent the number of obstacles in a randomly selected game. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U\\{80,81,…,125\\},$ and we wish to compute $\\text{SD}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U\\{a,a+1,…,b\\},$ then the variance of $X$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{|S{|}^{2}-1}{12}\n$$\n\nwhere $S=\\{a,a+1,…,b\\}.$\n\nNow, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|S| & =b-a+1 \\\\  & =125-80+1 \\\\  & =46.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U\\{80,81,…,125\\},$ we have the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{{46}^{2}-1}{12}=\\frac{2\\,115}{12}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\frac{2\\,115}{12}}≈13.28.\n$$"}]}
